# 4. Prompt Evaluation vs Model Evaluation

These two concepts are related but different.

| Basis | Prompt Evaluation | Model Evaluation |
|---|---|---|
| Meaning | Evaluates the quality of a prompt | Evaluates the performance of an AI model |
| Focus | Instructions and input design | Model capabilities and performance |
| Objective | Find the most effective prompt | Find how well a model performs |
| Changes | Prompt is modified | Model, training, or configuration may be changed |
| Example | Comparing two prompts for summarization | Comparing two language models |

### Example

Suppose we use the same AI model with two prompts.

- Prompt A: Explain machine learning.
- Prompt B: Explain machine learning in 100 words with one practical example.

If Prompt B gives more useful results for our intended task, it may be a better prompt.

The model remains the same. Only the prompt changes.

