# 16. Common Prompt Failures

During evaluation, several common problems may appear.

| Problem | Explanation | Possible Improvement |
|---|---|---|
| Ambiguity | Prompt has unclear instructions | Use specific language |
| Hallucination | Model generates unsupported information | Provide reliable context and require uncertainty handling |
| Inconsistency | Similar inputs produce different quality responses | Improve instructions and test repeated runs |
| Irrelevance | Response does not answer the question | Define the task clearly |
| Incomplete Output | Important information is missing | List required output elements |
| Formatting Errors | Output does not follow requested format | Specify a strict output structure |
| Excessive Length | Response contains unnecessary details | Add length constraints |
| Bias | Output may show unfair assumptions | Test diverse inputs and review results |
| Instruction Failure | Model ignores some requirements | Make important requirements explicit |

### Example: Ambiguous Prompt

Poor prompt:

```text
Tell me about Java.
```

Improved prompt:

```text
Explain Java programming language to a beginner.
Include its definition, three features, and one simple example.
Use easy language.
```

The improved prompt reduces ambiguity and provides measurable expectations.

