# 20. Advantages and Limitations of Prompt Evaluation

### Advantages

- Improves the quality of AI-generated responses.
- Helps identify weaknesses in prompts.
- Increases consistency and reliability.
- Reduces incorrect or irrelevant outputs.
- Helps compare different prompt versions.
- Supports systematic prompt improvement.
- Can reduce unnecessary token usage and costs.

### Limitations

- Some generated responses are difficult to evaluate objectively.
- Human evaluation requires time and effort.
- Automated metrics may not understand context.
- LLM judges can introduce their own biases.
- Results may change across model versions or settings.
- A small evaluation dataset may not represent real-world usage.
- A high evaluation score does not guarantee perfect performance in every situation.

